  "rationale": "The batch repeatedly uses a noun after a determiner and optional adjective(s), but the scissors output root lacks the corresponding determiner-plus-adjectives rule present for other object nouns. This leaves contexts such as “The small” with scissors at near-zero probability despite the noun continuation being structurally supported. Add that reusable noun-phrase pattern for scissors. The batch also has proper names after comma-terminated introductory phrases; a generic comma-suffix rule supplies evidence for each available name without deciding which name must follow. Commas can also precede non-name material, and any of the names may be valid here, so these rules add probability mass rather than making other continuations impossible.",
